# f1 = byShift, f2 = byIndex, f3 = ofOthers
# A layout whose objects never reach unseen code is not tested for at what comes out of unseen code: such a guess can never hold. What a method of a list hands out bears the seed of contents that nobody follows, and that seed
# counts as unseen code; but a list made in this body holds what this body puts into it. The layouts that the body's own text puts into the list (its elements at birth, push, a store by key) stay in the expectation:
# what the list hands out is asked for the layout once, and the fields are read by their slots.
# RUN(SHIFT): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# SHIFT: = ShapeTest
# SHIFT: = GetSlot {{*}}key="node"
# SHIFT: = GetSlot {{*}}key="steps"
# What is read by an index off such a list is proven, as before: no test and no read by name.
# RUN(INDEX): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# INDEX: code f2:Body
# INDEX-NOT: = PropGet
# RUN(PROVEN): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# PROVEN: code f2:Body
# PROVEN-NOT: = ShapeTest
# A list made here into which the body puts other things alone is asked for no layout of the file, though one has the names: the reads stay reads by name that ask the structure first.
# RUN(OTHERS): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# OTHERS: code f3:Body
# OTHERS: = CallBuiltin {{*}}overload=ArrayPrototypeShift/0
# OTHERS-NOT: = ShapeTest
# OTHERS: = PropGet {{*}}key="knot"
